│                                                                                                         │
│ Typical flow:                                                                                           │
│ 1. Intake and triage                                                                                    │
│    - The customer reports the issue.                                                                    │
│    - The system captures relevant details: account, transaction(s), timing, device/location context,    │
│ and reason for concern.                                                                                 │
│    - The case is classified by severity and urgency.                                                    │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 2. Immediate protective controls                                                                        │
│    - Potentially risky activity may be temporarily restricted.                                          │
│    - Extra authentication may be required.                                                              │
│    - Cards, transfers, or account access may be limited if compromise is suspected.                     │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 3. Automated screening                                                                                  │
│    - Fraud/risk systems evaluate patterns, recent activity, sanctions/AML indicators, and account       │
│ history.                                                                                                │
