│ 4. HITL review by a qualified banking professional                                                      │
│    - A trained fraud, disputes, or security specialist reviews the case.                                │
│    - They validate whether the alert is legitimate, false positive, or requires escalation.             │
│    - They assess customer impact, regulatory obligations, and whether additional evidence is needed.    │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 5. Customer verification and evidence gathering                                                         │
│    - The specialist may contact the customer through approved channels.                                 │
│    - They confirm disputed transactions, recent account activity, device usage, travel, merchant        │
│ interactions, and possible credential compromise.                                                       │
│    - Supporting documents or statements may be collected.                                               │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 6. Decision and action                                                                                  │
